;; DESIGN-045-wikilink-predicate-language: a predicate language for wikilinks
;; Research and design plan producing SPEC-045-wikilink-predicate-language
;; (specification) and IMPL-045-wikilink-predicate-language (implementation
;; plan, scaffolded but NOT executed).
;;
;; Scope: USDD Phase 1 (Vision -> Specification) + Phase 2 (Specification ->
;; Plan). OUT OF SCOPE: code generation. This plan ends at "human-review
;; package delivered + IMPL-045 drafted." Phase 3 begins only after the spec
;; reaches status=approved and a human reviewer signs off.
;;
;; Source: the Christopher Allen "Wikilinks and Named Edges" reference guide
;; (gist 151aefa6a6bde1ce4fa6b1182656cebe). The strawman seeded by the kickoff
;; session already exists at specs/SPEC-045-wikilink-predicate-language.md
;; (status=draft, version 0.1.0-strawman). This plan graduates it.
;;
;; SIBLING: SPEC-044 (Concept Graph -- SPO Relations, Emergent Vocabulary,
;; In-Situ Ratification, by the m3-kairos dyad + Mat Mytka) is the vision/UX
;; spec for the SAME capability, authored independently against the same gist.
;; SPEC-045 is its engineering companion. The two diverge on the authoring
;; surface (SPEC-044: frontmatter relations: ; SPEC-045: body-inline
;; predicate::[[Target]]) and on the telos of annotations (SPEC-044 declines
;; the agent-reading-budget framing as connective-not-conjunctive). Per the
;; user's 2026-06-09 direction, SPEC-045 is KEPT AS A SIBLING (renumbered from
;; the colliding SPEC-043, which is the .zetlignore corpus-view spec) and
;; DEFERS to SPEC-044 on both divergences. Reconciling the two is the first,
;; gating task of this plan (task-reconcile-spec-044).
;;
;; Review tier: Tier 2. Two factors push it above standard feature code:
;;   (1) it changes the core graph semantics every other feature reads, and
;;   (2) the SPL fact projection introduces a NEW trust boundary -- a predicate
;;       on page A asserts a fact ABOUT page B (Threat Model A in the spec).
;; Per USDD Multi-Model Cognitive Diversity, Tier 2 mandates cross-model review
;; + human review. The named-edge recogniser is a parser at a trust boundary,
;; so fuzzing is a mandatory deliverable; the fact projection is a transform,
;; so a roundtrip property test is a mandatory deliverable.

(meta plan
  (id "DESIGN-045")
  (title "A predicate language for wikilinks")
  (version "0.1.0")
  (status "draft")
  (created "2026-06-09")
  (author "agent:claude")
  (spec "SPEC-045")
  (description "Research and design a predicate language for zetl wikilinks: typed named edges of the shape predicate::[[Target]] layered additively on the existing [[wikilink]] graph, per the Christopher Allen 'Wikilinks and Named Edges' guide. Core design moves to validate: (a) recognise the predicate at the existing parse boundary and attach it as an OPTIONAL field on the Wikilink AST node, so a bare wikilink is a named edge with a null predicate (full backward compat by construction); (b) carry the predicate through the LinkGraph as edge metadata, typing backlinks/dead-links/orphans; (c) govern the vocabulary as a curated folksonomy (.zetl/predicates.toml; undeclared predicate WARNS, never errors) seeded with the guide's five categories; (d) expose a zetl edges query surface; (e) under --features reason, project each typed edge to a provenance-tagged SPL fact (predicate src tgt), making the typed graph queryable by the existing defeasible engine -- the same sugar-over-SPL pattern SPEC-042 used for public_paths. The new trust boundary (page-authored facts about other pages) is the spec's primary security concern and the reason for Tier 2. Outputs: specs/SPEC-045-wikilink-predicate-language.md (graduated strawman->approved), the concept pages it dead-links to ([[Wikilinks and Named Edges]], [[Security Form Contract]], [[Deep Context Architecture]]), /users/gardener/{user,happy-paths}.md and the other profile files, ADR-### records, CON-### contracts, TEST-### specifications, threat model, cross-model adversarial review, human-review package, and plans/IMPL-045-wikilink-predicate-language.spl scaffolded for downstream implementation. NO CODE IS WRITTEN UNDER THIS PLAN."))

;; -- Agents --------------------------------------------
(given agent-claude-available)

;; -- Tasks ---------------------------------------------

