;; -- Task Metadata -------------------------------------

(meta task-reconcile-spec-044
  (description "FIRST, GATING TASK. Reconcile SPEC-045 with its sibling SPEC-044 (Concept Graph -- SPO Relations, Emergent Vocabulary, In-Situ Ratification; specs/SPEC-044-concept-graph-spo-emergent-vocabulary.md) before any other Phase-1 work proceeds. SPEC-044 already metabolised the same Christopher Allen gist (its section 9 adopt/translate/decline). Resolve the two real divergences and record the resolutions in BOTH specs: (1) AUTHORING SURFACE -- SPEC-044 chose frontmatter relations: as canonical and flagged body-inline predicate::[[Target]] as an open Tier-1 fork (SPEC-044 section 9.2). Decide the canonical store and the relationship between the two surfaces: (A) frontmatter-canonical + prominent render (SPEC-044 default), (B) body-inline canonical, (C) author inline AND derive/mirror to frontmatter. SPEC-045 currently DEFERS to SPEC-044; if the decision is (A), re-scope SPEC-045 REQ-4501 so body-inline is an optional in-prose affordance that compiles to the same triple, not the canonical surface. (2) TELOS of annotations -- SPEC-044 section 9.3 declines the agent-reading-budget framing; adopt SPEC-044's answerability framing for the note/annotation and purge the budget-optimiser language from SPEC-045 prose (the machine contracts are telos-neutral and unaffected). ALSO: confirm the division of layers (SPEC-044 = vision/UX/governance/ratification; SPEC-045 = grammar/AST/graph/projection/CLI/tests/threat-model) with Mat / the m3-kairos dyad, and agree which artefact IDs each spec owns so they do not collide. Produce a short reconciliation note linking both specs.")
  (acceptance "research/SPEC-044-045-reconciliation.md exists recording: the authoring-surface decision (A/B/C) with rationale and sign-off from a SPEC-044 author; the telos decision; the layer-ownership table; any SPEC-045 REQ re-scoping required. SPEC-045 section 1.2 and SPEC-044 (a cross-link to SPEC-045) are both updated to reflect the agreed split. No artefact-ID collisions remain between the two specs.")
  (trace "SPEC-045 section 1.2; SPEC-044 section 9"))

(meta task-survey-parse-boundary
  (description "Survey how zetl recognises [[wikilinks]] and ![[embeds]] today, so the predicate recogniser slots into the EXISTING scan rather than adding a second pass (SPEC-045 REQ-4501). Cover: the regex extraction in src/scanner.rs:394-492; the post-parse split_wikilinks() in src/hooks/ast/parse.rs:683-767 and its KNOWN multibyte byte-index gotcha (em-dash/any multibyte char panics -- this is a fuzzing-relevant hazard for Threat Model B); the Wikilink struct fields in src/hooks/ast/mod.rs:419-425 (target/alias/heading/block_id). Identify the precise insertion point where a predicate:: prefix would be detected and where code/frontmatter/HTML-comment exclusion already happens. Document whether list-item-form vs inline-form edges are distinguishable at this layer (REQ-4504 annotation capture depends on it).")
  (acceptance "research/SPEC-045-parse-boundary.md exists with file:line citations for the two extraction sites, the exact recogniser insertion point, an explicit statement on the multibyte-panic hazard and its test implication, and a determination on whether annotations (list-item nested content) are reachable at the parse layer or must be captured at the graph layer.")
  (trace "SPEC-045 REQ-4501 CON-4501"))

(meta task-survey-graph-internals
  (description "Survey the LinkGraph so the predicate dimension lands cleanly (SPEC-045 REQ-4506). Cover: LinkGraph and EdgeMeta in src/graph.rs:10-26 (the fields EdgeMeta carries today: source_file, line, alias, heading, block_ref, is_embed); BacklinkResult at src/graph.rs:34-41; build() phantom-node mechanism at src/graph.rs:122 (basis for typed ghost edges, REQ-4514); backlinks() at src/graph.rs:190; dead_links() at src/graph.rs:212; orphans() at src/graph.rs:236. Determine the cheapest way to add predicate + annotation to EdgeMeta and a predicate-keyed index for the NFR-4502 query-latency budget.")
  (acceptance "research/SPEC-045-graph-internals.md exists with file:line citations; a concrete shape for the EdgeMeta extension; a recommendation for the predicate index (build-time vs lazy) with the NFR-4502 budget cited; confirmation that orphan/dead-link counts are unchanged by typing (only the reported metadata grows).")
  (trace "SPEC-045 REQ-4506 REQ-4514 NFR-4502"))

(meta task-survey-reason-projection
  (description "Survey how page content reaches the reasoner so named-edge -> SPL fact projection (SPEC-045 REQ-4510, CON-4504) is faithful and provenance-preserving. Cover: the theory pipeline in src/reason/mod.rs:72-150 (parse each SplBlock via spindle_parser::parse_spl, the provenance-annotation step at src/reason/mod.rs:116-145 that injects _source_file/_source_line/_source_page, the fact-relabel-to-__fact_N collision avoidance at 127-146); SplBlock extraction at src/scanner.rs:224-243 and the struct at src/types.rs:5-21. Determine how to inject synthetic facts (predicate src tgt) into the same theory with the SAME provenance machinery, and confirm the predicate grammar (lowercase-snake) is a valid SPL functor. CRITICAL: this is the Tier-2 trust boundary -- document how a consuming rule can scope trust by _source_page (Threat Model A).")
  (acceptance "research/SPEC-045-reason-projection.md exists with file:line citations; a concrete injection point for projected facts; confirmation the provenance path applies to synthetic facts; a worked example of a rule scoping trust by _source_page; an explicit note on determinism/order-stability of the projected fact set.")
  (trace "SPEC-045 REQ-4510 CON-4504 ThreatModelA"))

(meta task-survey-ast-evolution
  (description "Survey the SPEC-032 zetl-ext AST additive-evolution rules so the Wikilink predicate field (SPEC-045 REQ-4503, CON-4505) is compatible. Cover: tools/zetl-ast-schema-v1.json Wikilink def and its required-set; the additive-only-within-major-1 rule (SPEC-032 NFR-3206); the round-trip validation in tests/ast_schema_integration.rs; how a predicate-unaware hook must round-trip the node byte-stably. Determine: does adding an OPTIONAL property (null default, NOT in required) preserve all existing hook contracts? Should the schema carry pattern ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$ on predicate as defence-in-depth? Confirm the ast_version minor bump (1.0 -> 1.1) is the correct evolution step and what consumes ast_version.")
  (acceptance "research/SPEC-045-ast-evolution.md exists with file:line citations; a yes/no determination on additive-compatibility with rationale; a recommendation on the schema-level pattern constraint; the exact ast_version bump and the list of round-trip tests that must gain a predicate case.")
  (trace "SPEC-045 REQ-4503 CON-4505"))

(meta task-prior-art-typed-links
  (description "Survey prior art in typed/semantic links over wiki/markdown graphs to pressure-test SPEC-045's design choices. Cover at minimum: Obsidian Dataview inline fields (key:: value) and how it differs from edge-to-page predicates; Logseq block/page properties; Semantic MediaWiki property::value and [[property::target]]; RDFa/JSON-LD typed relations; Roam attributes. For each: syntax, where the type lives (frontmatter vs body vs inline), whether the type is a first-class graph edge or a property, query surface, and vocabulary governance (open vs closed). Extract lessons that confirm or challenge: predicate-binds-to-link (REQ-4501), body-not-frontmatter (ADR-4505), curated-folksonomy (ADR-4502), conforms_to-over-is_a (ADR-4503).")
  (acceptance "research/SPEC-045-prior-art-typed-links.md exists with a comparison table (>= 5 systems x the dimensions above); an explicit per-system 'lesson for SPEC-045' column; at least two findings that CHALLENGE a current strawman decision (or a recorded statement that none do, with reasoning).")
  (trace "SPEC-045 section 1 ADR-4501 ADR-4502 ADR-4503 ADR-4505"))

(meta task-prior-art-vocab-governance
  (description "Survey vocabulary-governance approaches for the curated-folksonomy model (SPEC-045 REQ-4507, REQ-4508, ADR-4502). Cover: the 'Wikilinks and Named Edges' guide's five curation activities (awareness, review, consolidation, clarification, enforcement) and its anti-ontology stance; folksonomy-vs-ontology literature; how linters surface lexical drift (nearest-match suggestions, Levenshtein thresholds); the guide's relates_to:: trap and is_a::->conforms_to:: argument. Determine the seed vocabulary content for .zetl/predicates.toml (the ~30 predicates across five categories, with display labels, the construction=true marker for extracted_from::, the catch_all=true marker for relates_to::, and the accept_is_a escape hatch).")
  (acceptance "research/SPEC-045-vocab-governance.md exists with: the finalised seed vocabulary (category -> predicates with display labels); a justified Levenshtein threshold for predicate-undeclared nearest-match; a justified default threshold for the relates_to:: over-use lint; confirmation that warn-not-error honours the guide's folksonomy stance.")
  (trace "SPEC-045 REQ-4507 REQ-4508 CON-4502 ADR-4502"))

(meta task-user-profiles
  (description "Build grounded user profiles per the USDD Synthetic User Protocol, refining the strawman sketches in SPEC-045 section 2: The Knowledge Gardener (maintains a long-lived vault, wants typed backlinks + vocab hygiene), The Traversing Agent (LLM building context under a reading budget, wants progressive disclosure + machine-readable typed edges + fact provenance), The Reasoning Author (writes SPL over the vault, wants faithful provenance-tagged projection), The Vocabulary Curator (audits and prunes the predicate vocabulary). Each profile names constraints precisely (e.g. 'CLI-fluent; comfortable editing markdown by hand; NOT assumed to know SPL').")
  (acceptance "/users/gardener/user.md, /users/traversing-agent/user.md, /users/reasoning-author/user.md, /users/vocab-curator/user.md exist in the Synthetic User Protocol template; constraints precise; each profile states which SPEC-045 surface it primarily exercises.")
  (trace "SPEC-045 section 2"))

